@auth @mock_github
Feature: GitHub Account Connection # features/auth/github_connect.feature:2
  As an authenticated user
  I want to connect my GitHub account
  So that I can sync my confabs to GitHub repositories
  @auth @mock_github
  Feature: GitHub Account Connection  # features/auth/github_connect.feature:2

  @positive
  Scenario: Successfully connect GitHub account                        # features/auth/github_connect.feature:13
    Given the API is available                                         # steps/common_steps.py:16
    And I am logged in as "user@example.com"                           # steps/common_steps.py:32
    And GitHub API is mocked                                           # steps/github_steps.py:15
    When I connect my GitHub account with:                             # steps/auth_steps.py:243
      | github_id | github_username | access_token   | selected_repo |
      | 12345     | testuser        | ghp_test123456 | confabs       |
    Then the response status should be 200                             # steps/common_steps.py:63
    And the response should contain message "GitHub account connected" # steps/common_steps.py:133

  @positive
  Scenario: Connect GitHub account with organization                   # features/auth/github_connect.feature:21
    Given the API is available                                         # steps/common_steps.py:16
    And I am logged in as "user@example.com"                           # steps/common_steps.py:32
    And GitHub API is mocked                                           # steps/github_steps.py:15
    When I connect my GitHub account with:                             # steps/auth_steps.py:243
      | github_id | github_username | access_token   | selected_repo | selected_org |
      | 12345     | testuser        | ghp_test123456 | confabs       | my-org       |
    Then the response status should be 200                             # steps/common_steps.py:63
    And the response should contain message "GitHub account connected" # steps/common_steps.py:133

  @positive
  Scenario: Update existing GitHub connection        # features/auth/github_connect.feature:29
    Given the API is available                       # steps/common_steps.py:16
    And I am logged in as "user@example.com"         # steps/common_steps.py:32
    And GitHub API is mocked                         # steps/github_steps.py:15
    Given I have already connected my GitHub account # steps/auth_steps.py:105
    When I connect my GitHub account with:           # steps/auth_steps.py:243
      | github_id | github_username | access_token    | selected_repo |
      | 12345     | testuser        | ghp_newtoken789 | new-repo      |
    Then the response status should be 200           # steps/common_steps.py:63
    And the GitHub connection should be updated      # steps/auth_steps.py:381

  @positive @wip
  Scenario: List available GitHub repositories     # features/auth/github_connect.feature:38
    Given the API is available                     # None
    And I am logged in as "user@example.com"       # None
    And GitHub API is mocked                       # None
    Given I have connected my GitHub account       # None
    And GitHub returns repositories:               # None
      | name    | full_name        | private |
      | confabs | testuser/confabs | false   |
      | private | testuser/private | true    |
    When I request my GitHub repositories          # None
    Then the response status should be 200         # None
    And the response should contain 2 repositories # None

  @negative
  Scenario: Connect GitHub fails without authentication  # features/auth/github_connect.feature:50
    Given the API is available                           # steps/common_steps.py:16
    And I am logged in as "user@example.com"             # steps/common_steps.py:32
    And GitHub API is mocked                             # steps/github_steps.py:15
    Given I am not authenticated                         # steps/common_steps.py:26
    When I connect my GitHub account with:               # steps/auth_steps.py:243
      | github_id | github_username | access_token   | selected_repo |
      | 12345     | testuser        | ghp_test123456 | confabs       |
    Then the response status should be 401               # steps/common_steps.py:63

@auth
Feature: User Login # features/auth/login.feature:2
  As a registered user
  I want to log into my account
  So that I can access my confabs
  @auth
  Feature: User Login  # features/auth/login.feature:2

  @positive
  Scenario: Successful login with valid credentials                      # features/auth/login.feature:14
    Given the API is available                                           # steps/common_steps.py:16
    And a user exists with:                                              # steps/auth_steps.py:24
      | email            | password   | name      |
      | user@example.com | SecureP@ss | Test User |
    When I login with email "user@example.com" and password "SecureP@ss" # steps/auth_steps.py:205
    Then the response status should be 200                               # steps/common_steps.py:63
    And the response should contain an access token                      # steps/common_steps.py:123
    And the response should contain user details:                        # steps/auth_steps.py:269
      | name      | email            |
      | Test User | user@example.com |

  @positive @wip
  Scenario: Login returns GitHub connection status                       # features/auth/login.feature:23
    Given the API is available                                           # None
    And a user exists with:                                              # None
      | email            | password   | name      |
      | user@example.com | SecureP@ss | Test User |
    Given the user has connected their GitHub account                    # None
    When I login with email "user@example.com" and password "SecureP@ss" # None
    Then the response status should be 200                               # None
    And the user should have GitHub connected                            # None

  @negative
  Scenario: Login fails with wrong password                                 # features/auth/login.feature:31
    Given the API is available                                              # steps/common_steps.py:16
    And a user exists with:                                                 # steps/auth_steps.py:24
      | email            | password   | name      |
      | user@example.com | SecureP@ss | Test User |
    When I login with email "user@example.com" and password "WrongPassword" # steps/auth_steps.py:205
    Then the response status should be 401                                  # steps/common_steps.py:63
    And the response should contain error "Invalid credentials"             # steps/common_steps.py:71

  @negative
  Scenario: Login fails with non-existent email                            # features/auth/login.feature:37
