@confab @mock_github
Feature: Delete Confab # features/confab/delete.feature:2
  As an authenticated user
  I want to delete my confabs
  So that I can remove unwanted AI agent configurations
  @confab @mock_github
  Feature: Delete Confab  # features/confab/delete.feature:2

  @positive
  Scenario: Delete confab successfully                       # features/confab/delete.feature:13
    Given the API is available                               # steps/common_steps.py:16
    And I am logged in as "user@example.com"                 # steps/common_steps.py:32
    And GitHub API is mocked                                 # steps/github_steps.py:15
    Given I have created a confab named "To Delete"          # steps/confab_steps.py:15
    When I delete the confab                                 # steps/confab_steps.py:331
    Then the response status should be 200                   # steps/common_steps.py:63
    And the response should contain message "Confab deleted" # steps/common_steps.py:133
    And the confab should no longer exist                    # steps/confab_steps.py:478

  @positive
  Scenario: Delete confab with documents attached            # features/confab/delete.feature:21
    Given the API is available                               # steps/common_steps.py:16
