@errors @validation
Feature: Validation Errors (422) # features/errors/validation.feature:2
  As the system
  I want to reject invalid input
  So that data integrity is maintained
  @errors @validation
  Feature: Validation Errors (422)  # features/errors/validation.feature:2

  @auth
  Scenario: Registration with invalid email format                 # features/errors/validation.feature:11
    Given the API is available                                     # steps/common_steps.py:16
    When I register with email "not-an-email"                      # steps/auth_steps.py:174
    Then the response status should be 422                         # steps/common_steps.py:63
    And the response should contain a validation error for "email" # steps/common_steps.py:102
    And the error should mention "valid email"                     # steps/common_steps.py:142

  @auth
  Scenario: Registration with password too short                      # features/errors/validation.feature:18
    Given the API is available                                        # steps/common_steps.py:16
